# The statements of trust-cg's e-graph rewrite rules over SemR, and their lemmas
# (PKG-U2; README.md). Compiled in order by the pinned `lean -o` (Lean's kernel
# checks them first): trust-ir's SemR — the `semr` family's `SemR.lean`, Clean's
# one copy of trust-ir `lean/semr/SemR.lean` (`from semr SemR`;
# `semr_reference.rs` pins its digest) — then the rule vocabulary (`EqsatRule`),
# the proof helpers (`EqsatBasics`), the statements that pin the vocabulary
# (`EqsatAnchors`), the two modules `gen_rule_defs.py` GENERATES from trust-cg's
# rule files (`EqsatIntRuleDefs`, `EqsatIntWrongRuleDefs`), the lemmas of the
# integer rule set (`EqsatIntSample`, then one module per lemma group:
# `EqsatIntArith`, `EqsatIntCmpSelBool`, `EqsatIntBitwise`, `EqsatIntNegRot`) and
# the refutations of the wrong rules (`EqsatIntControls`).
from semr SemR
EqsatRule
EqsatBasics
EqsatAnchors
EqsatIntRuleDefs
EqsatIntWrongRuleDefs
EqsatIntSample
EqsatIntArith
EqsatIntCmpSelBool
EqsatIntBitwise
EqsatIntNegRot
EqsatIntControls
